+1. **Feature Detection:** Compute the gradient magnitude $|\nabla v|$ for every voxel $v$ in $V$ using the central differences method [S1, S2, unofficial].
+2. **Axis-wise Filtering:** For each axis direction (X, Y, Z) sequentially:
+   a. For each pair of adjacent blocks $b_i$ and $b_{i+1}$ along the current axis, extract sets of axis-aligned samples $S$ traversing the boundary [S1, S2, unofficial].
+   b. For each set $S$, compute a rational Bézier curve using the samples as control points [S1, S2, unofficial].
+   c. Project the samples in $S$ onto this curve to compute filtered intensities [S1, S2, unofficial].
+   d. Update the voxels closer to the border (half the voxels of each block) with the projected values [S1, S2, unofficial].
+3. **Final Intensity:** For each voxel $v$, compute the final intensity $I_f(v)$ as the average of its three filtered values obtained from the X, Y, and Z passes [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
